# Production build config, embedded into the bundle by `vite build`.
#
# THIS FORK BUILDS OFFLINE-ONLY. With VITE_API_URL unset, api.isConfigured() is false
# and the client never touches the network: saves stay in local storage, and raids are
# resolved by the client's own simulation instead of being replayed by a Worker.
#
# It deliberately does NOT point at the upstream project's Worker, which is what it
# inherited. That server builds its raid verifier from UPSTREAM's combat code, and this
# fork keeps its own -- so every raid would either be refused outright (`stale_ruleset`)
# or, if the two ruleset numbers ever coincided, replayed under the wrong rules and
# settled against what the player actually watched happen. See RAID_RULESET_VERSION in
# src/raid/replay.ts.
#
# To go online, stand up a Worker FROM THIS REPO (server/, `npm run deploy`) and point
# VITE_API_URL at it, with a Google client id of your own. Client and server then share
# one ruleset number by construction and can never disagree.
#
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-own-worker.workers.dev
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-own-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
